{"change_summary":"Addressed the three pending amendments by removing the extra GH mineral multiplier from shrimp spawning and locking that behavior with a regression test, reworking the light-depth scenario into a nutrient-rich fast-stem comparison that now yields real net shallow plant growth while preserving the depth/light mechanism, and tightening the equipment-scaling concentration envelope from 55% to 40% while keeping the full habitat/geometry probe suite green.","outstanding_risks":["Mineral suppression now reaches spawning only through the smoothed reproductive-readiness EMA; if abrupt same-day GH shock suppression is required later, it will need a separate non-duplicated path.","The light-depth probe now depends on a curated fast-stem, nutrient-rich setup to keep the shallow run net positive; major plant-growth or light-model retunes may require refreshing those initial conditions.","The equipment-scaling probe is stricter at 40%, but the current DO-range divergence is still close to that envelope, so additional non-linear geometry retunes could push it over the threshold.","This pass reran the touched reproduction and habitat-probe suites, not the entire workspace test matrix."],"steps":[{"description":"Verified each pending amendment against the current implementation to confirm the shrimp mineral path was double-counted, the light-depth probe only showed differential decline, and the equipment-scaling envelope was too loose.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Patched shrimp spawning to rely on reproductive readiness once, and added a reproduction regression test that checks low-GH spawning tracks the readiness index instead of applying a second mineral penalty.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Rebalanced the light-depth probe so the shallow run achieves positive plant growth, added an explicit positive-growth check, tightened the equipment-scaling tolerance to 40%, and reran the habitat/geometry probe suite plus reproduction tests.","order":3,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo fmt --all` completed successfully.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test reproduction_factors -- --nocapture` passed: 15 tests green, including `test_mineral_suppression_is_applied_once_in_spawning`.","`cargo test -p tank_harness --test e2e_habitat_geometry_probes -- --nocapture` passed: 6 tests green, including `all_habitat_geometry_probes_summary` with 5/5 probes passing.","The updated light-depth summary now reports positive shallow growth versus deeper water (`0.6301 g` vs `0.2785 g`), and the tightened equipment-scaling probe still passes with the 1x vs 2x runs inside the new 40% envelope."]}